@target(py, js)
# The single audited exception boundary in portable code. JSON parse failures are
# host errors with no portable non-throwing API; a bare handler behaves identically
# in Python (`except Exception`) and JS (`catch`). See ADR-0001 and
# tools/exceptional.txt. Do not add another exception boundary without a parity test.

+@parse(text:s)->A?{
  !{
    ^@j(text)
  }!!e{
    ^N
  }
}
